+/*
+ * H629: the A540 panel test paints colour blocks into the same framebuffer this
+ * console draws text on, and those blocks were found replaced within seconds of
+ * being written. The display driver counts four writers and the console was not
+ * among them, so nothing tied the two together. These counters record what the
+ * console actually does to the panel: scrolls, glyph cells, screen clears and
+ * cursor flips, with the scroll region and text grid in effect. The display
+ * driver reads them once per heartbeat and reports the delta, so a change in
+ * panel content can be matched to a console write in the same beat, or shown to
+ * be independent of it. Nothing here changes behaviour; it only counts.
+ *
+ * [0] scroll_down calls      [1] scroll_up calls
+ * [2] text rows copied by scrolls   [3] bytes copied by scrolls
+ * [4] paint_char calls       [5] clear_screen calls
+ * [6] reverse_cursor calls   [7] last scroll region top
+ * [8] last scroll region bottom     [9] v_rows (text rows on the panel)
+ * [10] v_columns (text columns)     [11] ISO_CHAR_HEIGHT (glyph height, panel rows)
+ */
+unsigned long long video_console_panel_counts[12] __attribute__((aligned(16)));
+
